    "Placement of temporary epicardial pacing wires at the time of mitral valve surgery is routine due to the risk of postsurgical bradycardia. New approaches include using pacing pulmonary artery catheters for minimally invasive mitral valve surgery and temporary cardiac resynchronization using pacing wires for hemodynamic improvement. Left ventricular lead can be implanted post-CRT if necessary. Recommendations for tricuspid valve surgery include routine temporary pacing wires placement, permanent pacing for unresolved instability after surgery, and intraoperative placement in high-risk cases. The atrioventricular node relates closely to tricuspid valve interventions, and repair techniques aim to avoid node injury, with a significant percentage experiencing regurgitation.": "genes"
